## Inherited and trait API audit — consistent-hash callback

- The Phase 11 matrix incorrectly described Rust `HashFunction` as having no Java public equivalent. Pinned Java 5.5.1 `AllocateMessageQueueConsistentHash` declares `(int, HashFunction)`, and `HashFunction.hash(String)` returns Java `long`; Rust `with_hash_function(i32, Arc<dyn HashFunction>)` and `HashFunction::hash(&str) -> i64` are the corresponding API.
- `compat.RebalanceFixtures` invokes the Java custom-hash constructor, while `crates/rocketmq-classic-consumer/tests/rebalance.rs` differentially exercises it using Java-compatible `String.hashCode`. Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_11_OFFLINE_METHOD_MATRIX.md` to record the correct constructor mapping. No implementation gap was found in this slice.
- PASS: inspected the pinned Java 5.5.1 constructor/interface source and the existing invoked Java fixture plus Rust differential path; no fixture change was needed. `git diff --check` passes for the matrix/log update.
